        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Tekton's sockets are a well-specified, Taiwan-made range with unusually clear published details: chromium-vanadium chrome sockets with stamped markings, phosphate-finished impact sockets marked twice, and a warranty with no time limit and no receipt. Most of the line is 6-point, which suits most buyers.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Start with a 3/8-inch drive set in both depths and both measurement systems, buy impact sockets separately if you own an impact gun, and add 1/4- and 1/2-inch drive rails as jobs require. If you were looking for the 24335, it is a torque wrench that has been discontinued, and a current Tekton torque wrench is the replacement.
          </p>
